// A beamed group spanning several strings: the tab beam SLOPES to follow the fret
// contour (like LilyPond) rather than sitting horizontal above the highest digit —
// which would stretch the lower digits' stems and push an above-script into the
// staff. A high chord beamed with lower melody notes: the beam descends from the
// chord, so the melody stems stay short and the fermata drops clear of the notes.
title "Tab beam slope"
time 4/4
key c major

part m {
  instrument bass
  section A { <a c g>8 a a@fermata a e f g a | }
}

form main { A }

score main {
  staff m
  tab m as full
}

// ⚠ THE TAB ASKS FOR `as full` EXPLICITLY (2026-08-29). A tab beside a notation staff
// of the same part now defaults to `as numbers`, which draws no stems, beams, dots,
// tuplet numbers or ties -- and this book is ABOUT one of those, so without the clause
// it would keep passing while testing nothing it claims to.
